  "referenceWeightKg": 83,
  "notice": "Game model references only. These are concentration proxies or effect references, not measured clinical serum targets. A display band does not establish a safe dose. Read actual response, intended total amount and separate rate or combination hazards.",
  "projectionAssumptions": [
    "Constant medication rate actually reaching the patient; bag label and clamp position alone do not establish delivery.",
    "Zero starting concentration, default tuning and an 83 kg reference patient. Earlier doses and co-infusions change the result.",
    "Projection time is model time. Generalized and calcium/amiodarone Euler accumulators are approximated by continuous first-order curves unless the interface simulates the runtime timestep.",
    "Default and maximum rate controls are visualization examples and plot limits, not administration recommendations."
  ],
  "formulas": {
    "plateau": "admittedRateMgMin * inputFactor / effectiveClearance",
    "exponentialProxy": "k = 0.693 / halfLifeSec; level(t) = plateau + (initialLevel - plateau) * exp(-k * t)",
    "oneCompartment": "Vd = max(weightKg, 30) * volumeLPerKg; k = effectiveClearance / (60 * Vd); level(t) = plateau + (initialLevel - plateau) * exp(-k * t)",
    "clearanceModifiers": "For lidocaine, effectiveClearance = clearance * (shock ? 0.6 : 1) * (esmololProxy > 0.1 ? 0.7 : 1). Modifier product is bounded below at 0.05 in the runtime.",
    "easedInput": "Calcium and amiodarone first ease the admitted rate with 15 s onset and 35 s offset. Their accumulators then approach the plateau of that changing input.",
    "displayUnits": "mcg/mL is numerically equal to mg/L. Calcium inputFactor converts salt mass into elemental calcium. Magnesium preserves the configured game label without introducing a conversion absent from the runtime."
  },
